§ `Chapter 18 -- Forgery`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 463, 464.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.

§§ `Section 464 -- Making a false document or false electronic record`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 464(1)"
GIVEN d IS A `Document Making`
      f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `makes a false document or electronic record` IF
        (`the act is done dishonestly` f OR `the act is done fraudulently` f)
    AND (   (    d's `makes signs seals executes or affixes an electronic signature`
             AND d's `intends it to be believed that it was made signed sealed executed or affixed by or by the authority of a person by whom the actor knows it was not`)
         OR d's `without lawful authority alters a document or electronic record in any material part`
         OR d's `causes a person who does not know the contents to sign seal execute or alter`)

§§ `Section 463 -- Forgery`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 463"
@export Decide whether the document making constitutes forgery under Penal Code 1871 section 463
GIVEN d IS A `Document Making` @desc Making a false document or electronic record (s 464) with intent to cause damage or injury, support a claim or title, cause a person to part with property, cause a person to enter into a contract, or commit fraud or that fraud may be committed.
      f IS A Fault @desc The s 464 making must be dishonest or fraudulent.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes forgery` IF
        `makes a false document or electronic record` d f
    AND (   d's `intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person`
         OR d's `intent to support any claim or title`
         OR d's `intent to cause any person to part with property`
         OR d's `intent to cause any person to enter into any express or implied contract`
         OR d's `intent to commit fraud or that fraud may be committed`)

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes forgery` IF
        `constitutes forgery` (a's `document making`) (a's `fault`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

